<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dhana Dhanya Pushpa Bhara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as ধনধান্য পুষ্প ভরা</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Dhana Dhanya Pushpa Bhara&quot; (&quot;Lavished with a wealth of grains and flowers&quot;) is a patriotic song in Bengali composed in 1905 by the writer Dwijendra Lal Roy. On 20 July 1905 the British colonial government split the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> Presidency in two along communal lines, into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-bengal">East Bengal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, with a Muslim majority, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bengal">West Bengal</a>, with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> majority.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When the Constitution of Bangladesh was drafted in 1972, it was chosen over &quot;<b>Dhana Dhanya Pushpa Bhara</b>&quot; by Dwijendra Lal Roy.</blockquote><a href="/songs/amar-sonar-bangla">Amar Sonar Bangla</a></li><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Dhana Dhanya Pushpa Bhara</b>&quot; (&quot;Lavished with a wealth of grains and flowers&quot;) is a patriotic song in Bengali composed in 1905 by the writer Dwijendra Lal Roy.</blockquote><a href="/songs/dhana-dhanya-pushpa-bhara">Dhana Dhanya Pushpa Bhara</a></li></ul></section>
